        "why_justification": "Every cell's verdict and deciding document is graded, so a review refused on a silent reference, a review allowed over the vendor, a release history skipped and an omission read as absence each show on the rows they move. Entailed by: \"One row per feature row in `draft_comparison.md` and no other rows, in any order, with `feature_id` exactly as the draft writes it. Each row carries two cells for each product. `racklane_verdict` and `micaform_verdict` each take exactly one of `STANDS`, `OVERTURNED` or `UNVERIFIABLE`: whether Theo's entry for that product on that row survives the documents. `racklane_decided_by` and `micaform_decided_by` name the one document that decides that cell, by its short name in the house rules \u2014 `racklane_manual`, `micaform_page` or `review` \u2014 or `none` where the verdict is `UNVERIFIABLE`. Which document decides a cell is not a judgement call: the house rules rank the documents, say what counts as a document speaking to a feature, and name the deciding document even where another one agrees with it, so every cell has one answer.\"",
        "tag": "core"
      },
